{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008765-blood-sympathy-amount-of-info-that-can-be-conveyed","id":1008765,"title":"Blood Sympathy--amount of info that can be conveyed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T19:45:59-08:00","id":1008765,"title":"Blood Sympathy--amount of info that can be conveyed?","content":"According to the book: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Only the strongest ties \u2014 such as those between sire and childe \u2014 result in clear messages. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">So the specific scenario is that a player committed diablerie on a neonate (actually a total of 3 vampires in one game session) and i wanted to use blood sympathy to alert the neonate's sire to the act. So how much would the sire know considering the book says a &quot;clear message?&quot; Would the sire know exactly who did it? </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1485-robwolf","name":"RobWolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1485_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T20:58:04-08:00","id":1008792,"title":"","content":"Did the player assault the neonate and diablerize him or was it one of those situations where the player stumbles across the torpid vampire and decides to eat them? If it's a case of assault, the sire would very likely know what the attacker(s) and diablerist looks like or who it is if he's familiar with them, as he may &quot;see&quot; the attack through his childe's eyes while it's taking place. If it's the case of the player just taking advantage of the situation, the sire may or may not know, just a foreboding sense of their childe being consumed. But if you want to play up on the blood sympathy angle, the soul trapped in the diablerist while the Tainted condition is in effect could try and send a message to their sire either contacting their sire through their dreams or something creepier like have the soul take control of the PC long enough to call their sire and gloat about it and of course the player has no memory of what was said or done while being controlled but notices the lost time. Which could install a level of paranoia about being Dominated and used by someone else for some unknown purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T21:45:04-08:00","id":1008807,"title":"","content":"This particular vampire was trapped under a beam (long story) and when he saw the character approach he thought she was going to help. Instead she staked him while he was helpless, took him to a secret location and committed diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1485-robwolf","name":"RobWolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1485_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T22:31:52-08:00","id":1008822,"title":"","content":"I don't recall Blood Sympathy allowing the Sire to see through the Childe's eyes, but given the scenario you described, I'dsay Blood Sympathy could alert the sire that the neonate was in distress and their general direction and distance at the time they were pinned, as well as alerting the side when the neonate died and the appropriate direction and distance to where that happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T06:39:34-08:00","id":1008897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008765-blood-sympathy-amount-of-info-that-can-be-conveyed?p=1008807#post1008807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This particular vampire was trapped under a beam (long story) and when he saw the character approach he thought she was going to help. Instead she staked him while he was helpless, took him to a secret location and committed diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the scenario, then it's very likely the sire knows. He might have sensed something happened when the beam fell on his childe. Again when the character were staked, and finally again when consumed. Blood sympathy is a psychic power, how that information gets conveyed is up to the ST. I usually prefer olfactory hallucinations. But I had one character who was a geodetic specialist with the eidetic memory merit. She would either get locations by mentally seeing a map with the numeric coordinates superimposed on it and names or elaborate descriptions appear on a sheet of paper from a computer print fax or in a text message with the relative listed as the sender. (The ST had seen Future Diary recently.) Another time another character of mine got a mental image of a scale model of Las Vegas. There was a hotel pulled out of the display and it was held by her sire as he was crushing a figurine of her lover then her sire ate the figurine. Her sire had diablerized her lover and she had picked up on his smug attitude over killing his rival and knew it would infuriate my character and there'd be nothing she could do about it. (Until later...)<br /> <br /> If your player was the perpetrator, assuming either type of character is around/exists, it's possible the player's character has a sire or childe who also knows they diablerized someone as well. They may have picked up on the player's swirl of emotion during the act and decided to use blood sympathy to look in to see the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-27-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}